# Questions do not edit files

If the user asks a question — research, “do we have…?”, “will X work?”, “how does…?”, “did you…?” — answer from the repo and stop.

Do not edit, create, delete, rename, format, or revert files. Do not run commands that write (installs, generators, formatters, git commits).

Start editing only after they approve that change in a later message (“do it”, “implement”, “go ahead”, “fix it”). A question in the same thread is not approval. An earlier “implement” does not approve a new question.
